;
; P0-item-4 (ORDER-SIGNIFICANT paths) — the MULTI-COLUMN exact-dup guard. Two
; @key pragmas declaring the SAME ordered two-column path `[A, B]` are a
; parse-time reject (repeating one ordered path is the error). This guards the
; ordered-vector comparison specifically: a buggy flip that compared only the
; first column, or that mishandled multi-column paths, would let `@key(A, B)
; @key(A, B)` slip through. Its complement `@key(A, B) @key(B, A)` is ACCEPTED
; at parse (distinct ordered paths) — the whole point of the flip.
; Rejects during PARSE, before demand. The bound query exists so dropping the
; dup-path check flips this reject->accept (a LOST CHECK, not a masked one).
#message b_2(u64 X, u64 Y).
#local foo(u64 A, u64 B) @key(A, B) @key(A, B).
foo(A, B) : b_2(A, B).
#query q(bound u64 A, free u64 B) : foo(A, B).
